arm64: dts: imx8mp-evk: leave the on-board eMMC (uSDHC3) to the TEE

OP-TEE drives uSDHC3 from the secure world for its RPMB storage (fTPM
state). Linux probing the same controller reconfigures both it and the
card, so the two worlds would trample each other's transfers. The board
boots from SD and nothing in Linux needs the eMMC, so keep the kernel
off it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board configuration for the TEE-owned eMMC]

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mp-evk.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mp-evk.dts
@@ -953,7 +953,8 @@
 	pinctrl-2 = <&pinctrl_usdhc3_200mhz>;
 	bus-width = <8>;
 	non-removable;
-	status = "okay";
+	/* Owned by OP-TEE (RPMB secure storage); never touched by Linux */
+	status = "disabled";
 };
 
 &wdog1 {
